# How to cite this project. GitHub shows this file as "Cite this repository".
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "VeriMol: formally verified safety filters for AI-generated molecules, in Lean 4"
abstract: >-
  An early research prototype of a framework for safety filters for molecules,
  with checks that are proven in Lean 4. A rule about a molecular graph is
  stated as a short definition; a checker and a machine-checked proof that the
  checker is right are written for it; and a filter hands a molecule on only
  if its SMILES is read, the graph is sound and the rule holds. One filter
  with one rule is built, on a reader and writer for SMILES with a proven
  round trip. Claude Code, an AI coding assistant, wrote the program and its
  proofs under rules that the author set.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Dablander
    given-names: Markus
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Beneficial-AI-Foundation/VeriMol"
keywords:
